[[!meta title="FOSS-related talks"
        description="A reasoned list of past talks in public events about Linux and FOSS"]]
[[!tag foss talks linux]]

This is a reasoned list of slides I wrote and used in past events about Linux and FOSS.
Most are in Italian and were presented at local dissemination meetings.

I have been for some years the president of a local Linux Users Group (now
closed) in my town. We organized multiple times the local edition of the 
[Italian Linux Day](https://www.linuxday.it/) in the month of
October in various venues; therefore, I generally managed to make either
introductory presentations about Linux and free software or some more technical
presentations. Now sometimes I still participate to the same event as 
invited speaker. 

Occasionally, I also gave speeches for local meetings of the association, or
participated in events organized by others elsewhere.

Slides are generally in PDF format for simplicity, but in some cases animations
are not rendered correctly in such a format. In those cases, the only alternative
is to download the provided current OpenDocument Presentation (LibreOffice Impress)
format. Note also that such slides are quite old and the layout can have minor
glitches in their layouts, because of font rendering changes in the meantime.

If a different license is not specified within them, assume the slides are released
under CC-BY-SA-NC license.

